## Plans and docs paths

| Surface | Rule |
|---------|------|
| **PR / phase plans** | Use **`targetPlanPath`**, **`parentPlanPath`**, or other explicit spawn **`inputs`** — absolute or workspace-relative paths supplied by Mission Control |
| **Follow-up edits** | Reuse the anchored absolute plan path from the lane — do not re-derive from directory segments under `.sedea/operations/` |
| **New plan writes (nested post-cutover)** | When spawn **`inputs.plansBasePath`** is supplied, write new sibling/child plan files under that absolute directory — resolution priority and helper invocation: rule **30** § *Plans write path resolution* |
| **Docs reports** | Resolve write root per **Docs write root resolution** below; write on the **main hosting clone** only |

### Nested plans layout (post-cutover)

After the scope **Phase C cutover milestone** is active (Master Plan §7 Caveats + **development-process.md** § *Plans layout (nested post-cutover)*), new **`plan and deliver`** dispatches may anchor plan files under nested folders:

```text
.sedea/operations/<workspace-bound-scope>/plans/YYYY-MM/<unique-dispatch-slug>/
```

| Segment | Meaning |
|---------|---------|
| **`YYYY-MM`** | Developer local timezone month at first plan write for that dispatch (sidecar **`plansMonthBucket`** when set) |
| **`<unique-dispatch-slug>`** | Kebab-case dispatch title + 4-char hex suffix from Squad Leader **`plan-state.mjs dispatch-intake`** |

**Pre-cutover** and in-flight dispatches keep flat-root **`plans/`** behavior when **`plansBasePath`** is omitted or cutover is inactive — rule **30** § *Flat-root fallback*.

**Explicit plan paths unchanged:** **`targetPlanPath`** and **`parentPlanPath`** remain the authoritative anchors for *which* plan file to edit; **`plansBasePath`** governs *where new* sibling/child plan files land when nested layout applies.

### `plansBasePath` handover (binding)

Mission Control re-injects absolute **`plansBasePath`** from leader **`dispatchPlansHandover`** on every downstream spawn whose skill schema declares the input (rule **4** § spawn validation — host persists handover on first Squad Leader spawn that supplies nested intake).

| Priority | Source | Agent use |
|----------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | Spawn **`inputs.plansBasePath`** (host-injected from leader handover) | **`writeDir`** for new plan scaffolds when nested layout is active |
| 2 | Explicit **`targetPlanPath`** / **`parentPlanPath`** | Authoritative *which file* — dirname may imply write dir when **`plansBasePath`** omitted |
| 3 | Flat **`plans/`** root for active scope | Pre-cutover fallback per rule **30** |

**Forbidden:** relying on transcript prose alone for nested folder propagation; omitting **`plansBasePath`** on plan-writing child spawns when leader nested handover is active; forwarding flat-root write dirs when **`plan-state.mjs resolve-plans-write-dir --json`** returned non-null **`plansBasePath`**; reconstructing **`.sedea/operations/.../plans/YYYY-MM/<slug>/`** from directory scans, dispatch **mtime**, or “newest” nested folder heuristics — bind to **`dispatchId`**, explicit plan paths, and spawn handover instead.

### Docs write root resolution (binding)

Operational docs (PRDs, brainstorm reports, ad-hoc PRDs, requirements docs, triage reports) are written under **workspace scope-level `docs/`** only:

- **`operationsDocsDirectory`** — absolute path to `.sedea/operations/<workspace-bound-scope>/docs/` from lane identity or spawn **`inputs`**.

| Priority | Source | Write root |
|----------|--------|------------|
| 1 | **`targetPath`** (`manage`) or other explicit handover absolute path | That path (must be under `.sedea/operations/`) |
| 2 | **`operationsDocsDirectory`** from spawn **`inputs`** or lane identity | That absolute directory (workspace scope `docs/` under `.sedea/operations/`) |
| 3 | None resolvable | Return **`partial`** with `outputs.missingFields` naming the gap — **do not write** |

**Forbidden:** per-dispatch bundle `docs/` paths; **`bundleDirectory`** as a docs write input or resolution step; agents constructing `.sedea/operations/.../` path segments from **user-id**, **`joint`**, dispatch **mtime** heuristics, or “newest” folder scans. **Allowed:** host-supplied **`operationsDocsDirectory`** and explicit **`targetPath`** under `.sedea/operations/`.

**Path placeholders in documentation:** `` `...` `` inside path examples marks **omitted middle segments**, not a folder named `...`. Substitute the **handover-supplied** absolute path — never literal **`joint`** or a user-id segment you constructed yourself.

