## On-disk layout (host-internal — plans/docs only)

Sedea binds operations **plans/docs** to one **workspace-bound scope segment** under `.sedea/operations/` (host-internal). Agents must **not** construct or document user-id path segments — use **`dispatchId`**, **`operationsDocsDirectory`**, and explicit plan paths from spawn **`inputs`**.

| Subtree | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `plans/` | Plan union for this workspace scope — flat **`plans/*.plan.md`** at scope root **or** nested **`plans/YYYY-MM/<dispatch-slug>/`** post-cutover when **`plansBasePath`** handover applies |
| `docs/` | Scope-level operational docs |
| `dispatch/<epochMs>/` | **Abandoned legacy** filesystem bundles — product must not depend on them |

Legacy installs may still have `user`, `joint`, or per-user UUID scope folders — migrate with the customer script below.

